# Exception: preprocessing pipeline console logs (P0038).
# The `*.log` rule above is scoped to LaTeX build artifacts, but it also caught
# these. They are deliberate, versioned artifacts: they replace the console
# output the CSD notebook used to retain on save, so a step's printed diagnostics
# stay reviewable and diffable across runs rather than living only in a terminal.
!02_thesis_data/_02_preprocessing/nielsen/*/pipeline_step_outputs/*.log
# Exception: the feature inventory CSV is the machine-readable half of
# user-docs/reference/nielsen-feature-inventory.md. Versioning both together
# makes a Nielsen re-delivery show up as a reviewable diff.
!02_thesis_data/_02_preprocessing/nielsen/_shared_modules/nielsen_feature_inventory.csv
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/logs/
# External confidential code (Manifold/RU Graph Engine) — local working copy only
graph-engine/
*.jsonl
**\settings.local.json

# Thesis snapshots: ALL ignored. None of them are source.
#
# A snapshot is a derived mirror of the OneDrive .docx at one moment -- ~325
# generated .md files per export, regenerable at any time by re-running
# thesis_snapshot.py against the document. The .docx's own history already
# lives in OneDrive version history, which is the real record.
#
# Tracking them was tried twice and abandoned twice: first tracking every
# snapshot (1,306 files of derived markdown), then tracking one published
# folder under shared_snapshot/. Both bloated source control with regenerable
# output for no benefit git was providing.
#
# The README stays tracked -- it documents how to RUN the exporter and is the
# only place that does. It is documentation that happens to live here, not a
# snapshot.
06_thesis_writing/docx-exported-snapshots/*
!06_thesis_writing/docx-exported-snapshots/README.md

# Trained models: regenerable artefacts, not source.
# `train_and_persist.py` rebuilds every one in ~30s from the feature matrices
# and cv_params.json, so committing them buys nothing and costs a lot: the
# LightGBM/Ridge .joblib files are opaque binaries git rewrites wholesale on
# every re-persist (RTD alone is 10.3 MB), and a re-persist happens whenever
# tuning or selection changes. Same argument that keeps thesis_full.docx out.
#
# The metadata JSONs ARE tracked -- they are small, diffable, and record which
# model was served with which features, train boundary and q90, which is the
# provenance the thesis needs.
04_thesis_results/srq1/models/*_model.json
04_thesis_results/srq1/models/*_model.joblib

# Run-local marker written by run_both_horizons.py --resume. Records when the
# current suite run began, so a stage counts as done only if its artefact is
# newer. Machine state, not a deliverable.
.run_both_horizons.stamp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engineered feature matrices -- TRACKED DELIBERATELY (P0053, 2026-09-08)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The SRQ1 training suite kept being killed for memory on the laptop, so
# training moves to the VPS. These matrices are the ONLY data input training
# needs -- each carries its features, target and train/val/test split in one
# self-contained file (verified: nothing else is read at train time) -- so
# tracking them is what lets the VPS `git pull` and run.
#
# 32 files, 4.5 MB total. Size was never the obstacle.
#
# THEY CONTAIN NIELSEN DATA: brand-level monthly sales for 95 named Danish
# brands, under the confidentiality agreement with Manifold AI. Brian decided
# to track them with the repo's public visibility stated (2026-09-08).
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: the blanket *.csv and *.parquet rules above
# still exclude the raw extracts and every intermediate preprocessing step.
# Only the final engineered tier is un-ignored. Do not widen this.
!01_SRQ1_Model_Training/01_thesis_data/_03_engineered/bymonth/**/*.parquet
!01_SRQ1_Model_Training/01_thesis_data/_03_engineered/bymonth/**/*.csv
